1
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:10,500
We take definitely a credibly neutral approach

2
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,300
that a lot of other ecosystems disagree with.

3
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:14,778
Credibly neutral doesn't mean

4
00:00:14,778 --> 00:00:17,580
that we give every single team the same amount of resources

5
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:19,100
because that doesn't make sense.

6
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:20,976
But what we do is we double down

7
00:00:20,976 --> 00:00:22,869
on the teams that are able to show

8
00:00:22,869 --> 00:00:24,985
user retention and traction themselves

9
00:00:24,985 --> 00:00:26,600
because that's actually where

10
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:29,242
the resources and the attention will go the furthest.

11
00:00:29,242 --> 00:00:31,648
But actually making it like a level playing ground

12
00:00:31,648 --> 00:00:33,283
for everyone to get to that stage,

13
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:35,640
I would say that's kind of like the core thesis.
